        "timestamp": 1777380583,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Dozens of Gaza children arrive in Jordan for medical care Issued on: 28/04/2026 - 14:49 A new group of wounded or ill Palestinian children from Gaza have arrived in Jordan to receive medical care, the kingdom's army said on Tuesday. They are the 26th group of children transported to Jordan since the start of the war in Gaza in October 2023. The 81 children, accompanied by 108 family members, arrived through the King Hussein, or Allenby, border crossing between the occupied West Bank and Jordan, the army said in a statement. Mali PM urges 'not to panic' after coordinated attack by jihadists, separatists 28/04/2026 King Charles in US for state visit amid differences over Iran war 28/04/2026 Violence escalates in Colombia with dozens of attacks before presidential vote 28/04/2026 'Iranians believe they have upper hand because they can endure double blockade better than US' 28/04/2026 Who is Iyad Ag Ghali, Mali’s most wanted man? 28/04/2026 'Diplomatic challenge': King Charles to meet Trump, address Congress in bid to spotlight UK-US ties 28/04/2026 Accused media gala gunman charged with attempting to assassinate Trump 28/04/2026 Budget airlines first to cut flights as jet fuel prices soar 28/04/2026 Two French alpinists break Mont Blanc speed climbing record 28/04/2026"
